cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TE-Fed, please cite this software."
type: software
title: "TE-Fed: Correction with Source Evidence and Reuse by State Matching for Federated Semi-Supervised Multisensor Object Detection"
authors:
  - family-names: Sun
    given-names: Pinghan
  - family-names: Jin
    given-names: Wenquan
version: 2.6.1
date-released: 2026-10-19
license: AGPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  TE-Fed combines source-evidence correction and state-matched reuse for
  federated semi-supervised multisensor object detection. The code includes
  training, calibration, rendering, evaluation and analysis. Datasets, trained
  weights and manuscript experiment records are not distributed.
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - semi-supervised object detection
  - multisensor perception
